# Drafted by Gemini (R21 church), edited.

~ arrive
Narrator: The carnival music stops at the threshold as if cut with a knife, and tarps hang where windows will go. Before the altar, a stone knight twice a man's height turns his heavy head.
man_in_marble [angry]: Speak your names across the quiet of your minds, strangers. Why do you track the filth of that painted revel across my threshold?
* Tell him the truth: our friends are in the festival -> truth
* [Deception DC 14] Say we came to pray -> lie_ok | lie_fail
* Say nothing -> silent

~ truth
approve rook_coldwake +2 tobin_hayward +2 silas_vane -1: You told the Man in Marble the plain truth about your friends
man_in_marble [neutral]: Truth is a rare coin on a night of fools. Stand within these stones, then, and let the silence keep you whole.
set man_in_marble_met
-> END

~ lie_ok
man_in_marble [weary]: No one comes to an unfinished roof to pray while the pipes scream outside, yet I will not cast you out. Keep the quiet, and the quiet will keep you.
set man_in_marble_met
-> END

~ lie_fail
Narrator: The stone knight's carved lip curls in a cold, silent sneer that settles into your bones like winter frost. Yet he does not raise his blade to drive you back into the street.
man_in_marble [angry]: Keep your falsehoods behind your teeth while you stand upon this floor. The shelter holds, though you do not deserve its grace.
set man_in_marble_met
-> END

~ silent
approve rook_coldwake +1 lucan_houndstooth +1 delphine_ravelle -1: You met the stone sentinel's challenge with respectful silence
Narrator: Your silence meets his own, heavy as quarry stone and twice as cold. Slowly, the giant inclines his head a fraction of an inch, granting you the peace of the bare floor.
set man_in_marble_met
-> END

~ talk
man_in_marble [neutral]: My watch does not waver, travelers. Speak what you require before the noise outside grows bolder.
* Ask to rest here -> rest
* Ask about the festival -> about
* [if not flag.church_quest_asked] Ask what he needs -> offer
* [if flag.church_quest_asked and quest.the_silent_church == asked] How many have we brought? -> status
* Take our leave -> END

~ about
man_in_marble [neutral]: The fool's clamor cannot cross this threshold, though I am bound to the flagstones and cannot march against him. I have stood through older madness than his, and I shall stand when his ribbons rot.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Sound stonework, even with the whole festival baying outside.
-> talk

~ offer
man_in_marble [neutral]: The folk of this village dance until their soles bleed, trapped in the jester's glamour. Bring those you can wrench from the revelry into this nave, where their minds may mend.
* We will bring them -> accept
* Not now -> talk

~ accept
approve tobin_hayward +3 rook_coldwake +2 silas_vane +2: You promised to rescue the villagers trapped in the jester's revelry
man_in_marble [neutral]: Carry them through the doors by wit or by strength, and I shall guard their slumber.
quest the_silent_church asked
set church_quest_asked
-> talk

~ status
if flag.church_guests >= 3
man_in_marble [neutral]: Three souls now breathe easy upon the cold stone, free of the bells and the greasepaint. You have done enough to honor this shelter.
quest the_silent_church sheltered
else
man_in_marble [weary]: Too few rest within these walls while the streets remain choked with painted captives. Bring more of the village inside before the parade claims them all.
endif
-> talk

~ rest
man_in_marble [neutral]: Lay down your burdens upon the stone. The hours of the carnival do not turn within my shadow.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Slabs true, mortar dry, and no bells on the docket. Mind the turf.
Narrator: The quiet here is complete and deep, smelling only of damp mortar and cool dust. You close your eyes, and the ragged edges of your spirit knit back together.
heal 10d8 party
hit_dice restore all party
set church_rest_taken
-> END

~ hold_door
Narrator: Outside, a wall of painted dancers presses against the church timber, every face split by the same wide, unblinking smile as they shove.
-> hold_menu

~ hold_menu
* [Athletics DC 15] Brace the door -> hold_ok | hold_press
* [Persuasion DC 15] Talk the crowd down -> hold_ok | hold_press
* [Performance DC 15] Strike up a tune they must stop for -> hold_ok | hold_press
* [ends:the_silent_church] Let the Man in Marble bar the door -> bar
* Fall back from the door, for now -> END

~ hold_press
Narrator: The heavy oak shudders on its hinges, and the sheer weight of laughing bodies forces your boots backward across the flagstones.
-> hold_menu

~ hold_ok
Narrator: The fevered crowd breaks against the threshold like surf upon a cliff, stumbling back into the lantern light as the heavy doors swing shut.
man_in_marble [neutral]: You held the line where mortar and iron nearly failed. Take this old tithe from the altar box, with a sentinel's gratitude.
quest the_silent_church done
set church_door_done
gold +100
-> END

~ bar
approve tobin_hayward -4 silas_vane -3 lucan_houndstooth -3: You let the church door be barred and left villagers to the parade
man_in_marble [weary]: Stand aside, then, for I will not lose the souls already gathered under my roof.
Narrator: The Man in Marble drops the great stone beam into its brackets with a sound like a falling headstone. Those still outside belong to the parade now.
interject name:silas_vane: We just folded our hand and locked the poor sods out with the house.
quest the_silent_church barred
set church_door_done
-> END
